# Badger Builder conventions

Canonical product-workspace copy. When editing this plugin from the `grav-admin/` integration root, the parent rule [`.cursor/rules/badger-builder.mdc`](../../../../.cursor/rules/badger-builder.mdc) mirrors these points via globs.

## CSS

Keep styles in `assets/css/` — do **not** add inline `<style>` in JS unless explicitly requested.

| File | Purpose | Loaded by |
|------|---------|-----------|
| `assets/css/badger-builder.css` | Front-end section styles | `badger-builder.php` on public `badger-builder` pages when `built_in_css` is enabled |
| `assets/css/badger-builder-admin.css` | Admin2 sections field | `sections.js` `_ensureStylesheet()` when the field connects |

### Class naming

Use single-hyphen names only (no BEM `__` or `--`):

- Shared: `bb-section`, `bb-main`, `bb-btn` (markdown inline buttons)
- Front-end panels: `bb-panel-{type}`, `bb-panel-{type}-{element}`, modifiers as suffixes e.g. `bb-panel-filler-small`, `bb-panel-hero-align-left`
- Panel backgrounds: `bg-transparent` (plugin) plus theme utilities `bg-{slug}` from the active theme colours list
- Admin2 editor: `bb-admin-*` e.g. `bb-admin-card`, `bb-admin-field`, `bb-admin-field-quarter`

Admin CSS is lazy-loaded only in Admin2; public pages never download it.

## Panels

Panel schemas live in [`panels/*.yaml`](../../panels/) (builtins) and optional theme / `user/data` Local YAML. `PanelLoader` merges plugin → data → theme (whole panel replace by `id`). `PanelRegistry` exposes the merged set; the panels API enriches `*_background` selects from the active theme’s `colours` via `withBackgroundOptions()`.

### New panel checklist

1. `panels/{id}.yaml` — schema + defaults (or theme `badger-builder/panels/{id}.yaml` to override/add)
2. Theme `badger-builder/templates/sections/{id}.html.twig` — markup; use `bg-{{ bg }}` (default `transparent`) when applicable
3. `assets/css/badger-builder.css` and/or theme CSS — front-end styles
4. `badger-builder.yaml` + `blueprints.yaml` — enable in defaults and plugin settings (`enabled_panels`)
5. `README.md` — panel table / sample YAML
6. `admin-next/fields/sections.js` (+ admin CSS) — only if the editor needs a custom field row or new field type

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for Admin2, markdown, and theme-integration notes.
